WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.010
Wealth, fame, power...

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:05.910
Gold Roger,
the King of the Pirates,

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.220
attained everything
this world has to offer.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:12.090
The words he uttered just before
his death drove people to the seas.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:15.920
My treasure?
If you want it, you can have it!

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.490
Find it! I left everything
this world has to offer there!

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:26.840
And so men head for the
Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams!

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.740
The world has truly
entered a Great Pirate Era!

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:36.110
We're going to gather up
all our dreams

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:42.020
and set out in search
of something to find

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.520
ONE PIECE!

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:53.860
Compasses only cause delays

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:59.600
Delirious with fever,
I take the helm

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:11.710
If the dusty treasure map has
been verified, it's not a legend!

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:17.420
When it comes to personal storms,

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:22.720
simply ride aboard
someone else's biorhythm

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:26.390
and pretend it isn't there!

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:31.900
We're going to gather up
all our dreams

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:37.610
and set out in search
of something to find

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:43.850
A coin in my pocket,
and do you wanna be my friend?

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:49.220
We are, We are on the cruise!

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:50.950
We are!

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:53.120
Gum-Gum...

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:58.130
...Bazooka!!

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.560
Oh, no!

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.700
If I can get my arms and
legs out, the game is mine!

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:06.900
What?!

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:10.140
This is gonna end it... for sure!

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:23.590
He can be defeated by someone
with a spear of blind determination.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:30.730
I know an idiot who's holding back
that spear for a stupid reason...

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:41.270
All... Blue...

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:47.480
I'm the strongest man!!

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.620
Don Krieg... We lost.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.290
Chief Commander!

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:01.560
Thanks for everything, Sanji-san.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:05.890
When he wakes up, could you tell him...

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:11.230
Maybe... I can live
only a few more hours...

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:14.900
It's kind of stupid that I'm resolved
because I don't have much time left,

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:18.910
but this time, I want to do it with
my own will... in my own way...

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:21.910
Then, there'll be nowhere
for me to escape, right?

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:26.410
You don't have to think about stupid
things like fearing your enemy

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:32.590
or how to keep from getting hurt...
I learned it from that guy.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:36.620
Well, then! We gratefully
accept the boat.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.930
We don't have to return it, right?

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:42.100
Right. If you have the courage
to come here to return it,

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.530
try it, you small fry.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.940
He's right! Just keep
this in your brain!!

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:51.610
This is the sea restaurant
Baratie, where cooks fight!

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:55.310
Hmph! What a scary restaurant...

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:06.690
"Set Sail! The Seafaring Cook
Sets off with Luffy"

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.240
Ahh! My hat! My straw hat!!

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:26.910
It's right there.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.740
Huh? Oh, yeah. Here it is.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.580
So you're awake?

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.580
Oh? Where're those guys?

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:36.250
--They left... thanks to you.
--Me?

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:40.920
Ghin said, "I'll see you
again in the Grand Line."

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.260
Ghin did?

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:46.260
--To you?
--No, to you!!

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.800
Speaking of which,
since I drove them away,

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.940
today is my last day
to do chores, right?

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.440
Congrats.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.940
By the way, will you...

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:01.540
I'm not going!
I won't become a pirate.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:03.040
I'll continue to work as a cook here

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:06.880
until I get that damn geezer
to acknowledge my skills.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.220
Okay, then I give up.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.920
Your hand hasn't given up yet!

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:20.560
I can't leave here...
since they're all undependable...

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:26.070
But I'm hoping to go some day...
to the Grand Line.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:29.900
Then let's go now.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:32.570
It's not the right time yet.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:39.080
Say... do you know the All Blue?

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.250
No...

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:44.450
Oh, you don't?! It's a miracle sea!

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:50.260
The East Blue, West Blue,
North Blue, and South Blue...

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:54.560
Fish from all those
four seas live in that sea!

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:58.930
To us cooks,
it's a dream-like paradise!

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:02.540
That's what the Grand Line is like.
So, have you heard...

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:10.880
He looks so happy...

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.710
That idiot...

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:21.220
Guys!! Meal time!!

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:22.560
Aw, man...

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.230
We can finally eat!

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:26.230
Food! Food! Food!

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:34.240
Hey, where do we sit?

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.040
Where's our food?

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.910
There're no chairs for you.

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:42.580
Sit on the floor and eat.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:48.080
No chairs? That can't be true!
This is a restaurant!

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:50.920
Guess we can't help it...

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:53.220
They're acting kinda weird...

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:57.930
Hmph! Nothing new...

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:01.860
Hey! Who prepared
the soup this morning?!

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:03.870
Hey, I did it! I did! Isn't it good?

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:06.530
I made it especially good today!

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:10.670
I can't eat damn nasty soup like this!
What is this, pig feed?!

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:23.220
Hey, is human food not to your liking,
you damn racoon dog?

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:26.220
Ha! When it's this bad, it's art now.

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:28.260
It makes me sick to my stomach!

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:32.560
I'm sorry, but I'm really
confident about today's soup.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:34.900
There's something wrong
with your taste buds!

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:42.240
Ugh! This is nasty!

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.940
I can't eat it!

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:49.240
Right, guys?!

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:51.910
I can't eat something like this!

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:53.920
This is damn nasty soup!

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:55.580
I can't eat soup like this!

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:58.250
This is terrible!
Someone, give me some water!

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:00.520
What do you think
you're doing, you bastards?!

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:03.360
You're a sham Sous Chef after all...

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:05.190
You're just an old-timer.

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:08.530
We're sick and tired of you
settling matters with violence!

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:12.530
If the food's bad, we're gonna say so!

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:14.470
What'd you say?!

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:22.010
We're seafaring cooks.
Don't waste even a drop of soup.

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:39.560
Owner!!

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:41.230
You geezer!

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:46.230
What is this damn nasty soup?
It's like sludge!

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:50.570
If we serve something like this,
our restaurant will go out of business!

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:52.410
Don't be ridiculous,
you damn geezer!

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:56.240
Just how is this soup
different from yours?! Tell me!

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:58.910
From my soup?

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.280
Don't flatter yourself!

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.190
Owner punched him...

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:08.890
He didn't kick...

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:15.030
It'll be a billion years before you can
give me a lecture on cooking, little brat!

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:19.400
I'm a man who has cooked
on seas around the world.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:31.050
Dammit!

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:40.890
That damn geezer! I... I...

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:44.790
I'm not a "little brat" any more!!

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:54.570
This soup is super good, you know...

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.900
--We know that.
--Huh?

00:09:56.900 --> 00:10:01.910
Sanji's cooking skills are
recognized by everyone here.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:02.910
It's not bad at all.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.910
Yeah, this soup is very well made.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:09.250
Boy, that was scary...
He seriously snapped...

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:10.750
Yeah...

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:22.430
But that idiot won't listen
unless we go this far...

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:25.600
--Say, kid...
--Hm?

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:28.940
You were saying that you wanted
a cook for your ship, right?

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:31.270
This isn't a favor that I'd
like to ask of you or anything,

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:36.610
but would you take that
little brat with you...

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.610
...to the Grand Line?

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:44.690
The Grand Line... is his dream.

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:49.290
Man, Owner, you really
made us put on quite a show.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:53.630
I was worried that he might figure
it out because of your bad acting.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:56.960
Your acting was horrible, too.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.300
I'll have another bowl of soup!

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:00.630
--Me, too!
--Me, too!

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:20.050
I can hear everything,
you damn idiots...

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:38.040
So what do you say, kid?

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.040
No.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:40.940
What?!

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:45.280
I thought you wanted
a cook for your ship.

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:49.950
Or are you saying that he's
not good enough for you?

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:54.960
He's good enough, all right.
I do want him to come with me.

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:58.290
But he says that he wants to
continue working here as a cook.

00:11:58.290 --> 00:12:02.230
Even if you guys ask me to
take him with me, I can't.

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:04.570
So you're saying that
you can't agree to it

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:07.570
until he tells you so himself, huh?

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:09.070
Exactly. More, please!

00:12:09.070 --> 00:12:11.910
Well... fair enough.

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:17.240
But who knows if that twisted
damn brat can just say he'll go...

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:21.250
There's no way he can, since he's
an idiot through and through...

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:22.750
More, please!

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:56.950
--Dammit!
--Sanji!

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:58.950
What is he? A fishman?

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:01.560
He came all the way from the
Fishman Island to eat our dishes?

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:03.890
Idiot! It's a human and a panshark!

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:05.390
Hm? What's going on?

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:07.560
Oh? Hey, it's you, Yosaku!

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:10.230
Oh, Big Bro Luffy!

00:13:10.230 --> 00:13:12.400
Why are you alone?
Where're the others?

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:14.600
What happened to Nami?

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:22.940
It's not that we caught up with her,

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:24.910
but from the direction
Big Sis Nami was heading,

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:27.920
we figured out roughly
where she was going.

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:31.590
I see... We can bring her back then.

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:40.160
Well... If what we're thinking is right,
her destination is a crazy place...

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:45.600
In any case, we need your help,
Big Bro Luffy. Please come with me.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:48.600
Okay! I don't really get it, but got it.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:50.340
I'll come with you.

00:13:57.950 --> 00:13:59.950
--Wait!
--Hm?

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:04.550
We both have foolish dreams.

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:06.050
Hm?

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:12.560
In order to achieve
my goal, the All Blue...

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:14.560
Sanji?

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:16.630
Yeah. I'll come along...

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:19.230
...on your journey to become
"King of the Pirates"!

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:21.240
What?

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:25.240
I'll be the cook for your ship.

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:31.910
Is that okay or not?

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:34.580
It's okay!! All right!!

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:36.420
I'm happy for you, Big Bro Luffy!

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:37.250
Yeah!

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:40.250
Yaay! Yaay! We got a cook!
We'll have good food!

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:44.590
So that's how it is, everyone.

00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:47.260
Sorry for causing you
all sorts of trouble.

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:53.270
Ha! I don't like it! I wanted to
kick you out from here myself.

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:57.270
And you decide it so easily?

00:14:57.270 --> 00:15:01.540
Sorry for making you
resort to bad acting.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.210
You knew?!

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:05.880
I could hear everything,
since you're all stupid.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:07.550
What?!

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:10.550
That is to say, you're willing
to go that far to kick me out,

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:13.220
huh, you damn geezer?!

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:18.230
Why do you always have to
talk like that?! You bastard!

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:22.560
Hmph! That's right, little brat!

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:25.070
I don't like kids to begin with.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:28.240
Not a single day passed
where I didn't regret

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.570
letting a useless one live,
you damn brat.

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:33.570
Ha! Fine by me, you damn geezer!

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:36.640
Enjoy the rest of your life to the utmost.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:46.590
Whoa! This is a nice ship.
Is it okay for us to use it?

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:49.260
Of course! It's Sanji's boat.

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.590
You still need more?!

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:53.260
Yeah. Give me more meat.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:56.260
Just how many days
will you be at sea?

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:57.460
Don't know...

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:00.530
--Kid...
--Hm? Pops!

00:16:00.530 --> 00:16:02.240
Do you wanna take this?

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:07.210
It's a record of my one-year
journey in the Grand Line.

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:09.380
Don't need it.

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:11.310
I knew it...

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.880
I want that marbled meat, too!

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:18.890
Enough already!

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:32.630
Whoa!! Damn geezer,
is this the sea restaurant?

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:37.000
"Baratie Employee Guidelines
1. Serving customers... That is 'love'!
And 'love' means 'restaurant'! 2. Motto! Motto! Service motto!"

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:55.590
For example, Sanji...

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:57.930
Hm? What is it?

00:16:57.930 --> 00:17:02.530
Be they arch rogues or jail breakers,

00:17:02.530 --> 00:17:04.970
if these damn bastards
badly want to eat

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:09.870
and find their way to this restaurant,

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:16.210
there may be a point in our
continuing to fight at this restaurant...

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:18.210
Yeah!

00:17:18.210 --> 00:17:20.880
We're gonna be busy!

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:23.950
We'll be fine 'cause I'm here!

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:28.060
Ah...

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:35.100
Uh! Ow! Ouch...

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:39.900
Geez...

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:42.570
You peeled the skin
too thick, little brat!

00:17:42.570 --> 00:17:44.570
That hurt!

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:48.910
When someone's cooking seriously,
you should just watch quietly!

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:51.910
What?! Don't get smart,
you little brat!

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:56.320
I'm not a little brat!
You damn geezer!!

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:00.520
Try this.

00:18:00.520 --> 00:18:03.190
Did you make it by yourself?

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:04.690
Yeah.

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:07.530
How is it?

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:11.200
Cripes, this is damn nasty,
you little brat!

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:14.070
You damn geezer!!

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:25.880
Big Bro Cook sure is taking time...

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:27.380
Yeah...

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:44.730
This is for my longstanding grudge!

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:46.730
Be prepared, Sanji!

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:56.210
There's no way you guys
can defeat him.

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:15.860
Let's go.

00:19:15.860 --> 00:19:17.870
You don't have to say goodbye?

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:21.030
--That's okay.
--Sanji!

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:24.770
Don't catch cold.

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:25.270
Owner Zeff!!

00:20:25.270 --> 00:20:26.770
Thank you for all the damn things

00:20:26.770 --> 00:20:29.940
you've done for me
over all these years!!

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:34.440
I'll never forget your kindness...
for the rest of my life!!

00:20:54.630 --> 00:20:57.330
You asshole!!

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:02.240
I'll miss you, dammit!

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:04.770
I'll miss you!!

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:19.920
I'll miss you!!

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:23.090
I feel sad, dammit!

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:32.270
You idiots!

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:36.470
Men should part without a word.

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:45.610
Let's go!! Set sail!!

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:49.980
I'll see you again, you damn bastards!

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:06.230
As long as you don't fear even death
because you have faith in yourself,

00:22:07.570 --> 00:22:13.770
you'll find the All Blue... for sure...

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:18.850
Guys! Customers are
gonna show up soon!

00:22:18.850 --> 00:22:22.280
Get to work already!

00:22:55.280 --> 00:23:09.530
When I was little, I had
a vision of a treasure map

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:16.470
and I always searched
for that miraculous place

00:23:16.470 --> 00:23:23.640
before someone else could
beat me to it

00:23:26.180 --> 00:23:37.660
If the world is going to change

00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:44.660
before I can even attain my dream

00:23:44.660 --> 00:23:51.740
then take me to the time
when I knew nothing

00:23:51.740 --> 00:24:05.120
so that my memories won't fade

00:24:10.220 --> 00:24:12.560
It sounds like Nami-san
headed to Arlong Park.

00:24:12.560 --> 00:24:13.560
What's that?

00:24:13.560 --> 00:24:15.560
It's a place dominated
by fishman pirates.

00:24:15.560 --> 00:24:16.900
She couldn't be...

00:24:16.900 --> 00:24:19.900
Considering her cuteness...
she might be a mermaid...

00:24:19.900 --> 00:24:21.230
--A water imp?
--I'll kill you!

00:24:21.230 --> 00:24:21.900
"Nami"
--A water imp?
--I'll kill you!

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:23.500
--Then a half fishman?
--No meals for you!
"Nami"

00:24:23.500 --> 00:24:23.570
--Then a half fishman?
--No meals for you!

00:24:23.570 --> 00:24:25.240
Why?!

00:24:25.240 --> 00:24:26.910
On the next episode of One Piece!

00:24:26.910 --> 00:24:30.580
"The Worst Man in the Eastern Seas!
Fishman Pirate Arlong!"

00:24:30.580 --> 00:24:33.380
I'm gonna be King of the Pirates!!
